[[!comment format=mdwn
 username="joey"
 subject="""comment 1"""
 date="2026-10-29T20:50:56Z"
 content="""
This has nothing to do with `git-annex info`, any git-annex command after
the first initialization behaves this way.

It seems that git-annex is seeing the git config
of "core.worktree=../../../../../../linked/sub" and getting a little bit
confused. 

It constructs a Repo with a location of eg

	Local {gitdir = "/home/joey/tmp/tmp.rQ1fokJzh0/linked/sub/.git", worktree = Just "/home/linked/sub"}

That worktree is wrong. And since it's not being run in that worktree,
it tries to chdir to it.

core.worktree is supposed to be relative to the gitdir. And
since `.git -> ../../main/.git/worktrees/linked/modules/sub/`,
that's "../../main/.git/worktrees/linked/modules/sub/../../../../../../linked/sub"
aka "../../linked/sub".

The wrong worktree comes from Git.Config.updateLocation. It is using the
gitdir seen above, rather than following the symlink to the git directory it points to.
So it uses "/home/joey/tmp/tmp.rQ1fokJzh0/linked/sub/.git/../../../../../../linked/sub"
which reduces to "/home/linked/sub".

So either Git.Config.updateLocation needs to change to follow the gitdir symlink,
or the symlink needs to be followed at an earlier point.

It's worth noting that the first time git-annex runs, it 
ends up with the correct location eg

	Local {gitdir = "/home/joey/tmp/tmp.D2wQYPhq9O/main/.git/worktrees/linked/modules/sub", worktree = Just "/home/joey/tmp/tmp.D2wQYPhq9O/linked/sub"}

So the trouble comes from the various fixups that git-annex init has to do
to convert .git files to symlinks.

I will need to refresh my memory about linked worktrees and gitdir symlinks to get
any further.
"""]]
